# ── Virtual environments ──
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Python ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Data (raw inputs + large generated intermediates) ──
data/raw_csv/
data/raw_csv_full/
data/raw_pcaps/
data/processed/*
# …but the paper split's PROTOCOL DEFINITION is small and is the provenance for
# every reported number (which classes are known, which are zero-day, exact row
# counts). Track it; keep the ~494 MB of arrays and meta CSVs out.
!data/processed/paper/
data/processed/paper/*
!data/processed/paper/split_report.txt
!data/processed/paper/known_classes.npy
!data/processed/paper/zero_day_classes.npy

# ── Trained models + fitted transformers ──
models/

# ── Large generated outputs (regenerable) ──
outputs/arrays/
outputs/embeddings/
outputs/predictions/
outputs/*.log

# NOTE: outputs/figures/ is intentionally NOT ignored — commit eval plots.
#
# NOTE: outputs/metadata/ is intentionally NOT ignored either (changed 2026-08-03).
# It holds `runs.jsonl` — the append-only research log backing EVERY number in
# docs/STATUS.md — plus small provenance artifacts (thresholds, class lists,
# modality_analysis.json, per-run history pickles). Total ~101 KB. While it was
# ignored, the entire research record had no version history, no backup, and no
# way to detect a corrupting write, even though KNOWN_ISSUES treats it as an
# append-only log that must never be silently rewritten. Nothing large belongs
# here — big per-run artifacts go to models/ or outputs/{arrays,embeddings,predictions}/.

# ── Copyrighted / reference material (do NOT publish) ──
basepaper.pdf
*.pdf

# ── OS / IDE ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
outputs/*.pid
outputs/*.log
